<header class="soc-head"><p class="featured-region">Social ladder · c. 600–371 BCE (to the defeat at Leuctra)</p><h1 class="soc-title">Social Hierarchy of Ancient Sparta</h1><p class="soc-sub">From Kings to Helots</p></header>
<div class="soc-intro"><figure class="soc-fig"><a href="/encyclopedia/leonidas-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonidas-i.jpg" alt="Leonidas I"></a><figcaption><a href="/encyclopedia/leonidas-i">Leonidas I</a><span class="soc-credit">de:Benutzer:Ticinese · CC BY-SA 3.0</span></figcaption></figure><p class="soc-lede">Classical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> was ruled by a small body of full citizens who lived from the labour of a far larger subject population. Rank rested on birth and law. A man of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartiates">Spartiate</a> birth who passed through the state upbringing (the agoge) and paid his dues to a common mess became one of the homoioi, the “equals”; poverty or cowardice could cost him that place. Two kings stood at the head of the state. Around the citizens lived the free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perioeci">perioikoi</a> in their own towns and several in-between groups: inferiors who had lost citizenship, foster brothers raised beside Spartiate boys, and freed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helots">helots</a>. At the bottom the helots, bound to the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laconia">Laconia</a> and Messenia, outnumbered the citizens many times over. The ladder was steep and almost closed: the citizen body shrank from about 8,000 men in 480 BCE to fewer than a thousand by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a>’s day.</p><p class="soc-facts"><span><b>Period</b> c. 600–371 BCE (to the defeat at Leuctra)</span><span><b>People</b> c. 250,000–350,000 (est.)</span><span><b>Ranks</b> 7</span><span><b>Profile</b> <a href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a></span></p></div>
<section class="soc-ladder-sec" aria-labelledby="soc-ladder-t"><div class="soc-ladder-head"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="soc-ladder-t">The ladder</h2><div class="soc-scale" role="group" aria-label="How to draw the ladder"><button type="button" class="soc-scale-btn" data-scale="0" aria-pressed="true">By rank</button><button type="button" class="soc-scale-btn" data-scale="1" aria-pressed="false">To scale</button></div></div><ol class="soc-pyr" data-scale="0"><li class="soc-row" style="--rw:24%;--k:0"><a class="soc-bar soc-b-ruler" href="#rank-1" style="--sw:0.4%"><span class="soc-bar-n"><span class="soc-loc">Basileis</span> <span class="soc-en">(The two kings)</span></span><span class="soc-bar-s">A handful</span></a></li><li class="soc-row" style="--rw:39%;--k:1"><a class="soc-bar soc-b-nobility" href="#rank-2" style="--sw:6%"><span class="soc-bar-n"><span class="soc-loc">Spartiatai</span> <span class="soc-en">(Spartiates)</span></span><span class="soc-bar-s">3–10%</span></a></li><li class="soc-row" style="--rw:54%;--k:2"><a class="soc-bar soc-b-commoners soc-est" href="#rank-3" style="--sw:2%"><span class="soc-bar-n"><span class="soc-loc">Hypomeiones</span> <span class="soc-en">(Inferiors)</span></span><span class="soc-bar-s">c. 1–3% (est.)</span></a><a class="soc-bar soc-b-commoners soc-est" href="#rank-4" style="--sw:0.4%"><span class="soc-bar-n"><span class="soc-loc">Mothakes</span> <span class="soc-en">(Foster brothers)</span></span><span class="soc-bar-s">c. 0.1–0.5% (est.)</span></a></li><li class="soc-row" style="--rw:70%;--k:3"><a class="soc-bar soc-b-commoners soc-est" href="#rank-5" style="--sw:20%"><span class="soc-bar-n"><span class="soc-loc">Perioikoi</span> <span class="soc-en">(Dwellers around)</span></span><span class="soc-bar-s">c. 15–25% (est.)</span></a></li><li class="soc-row" style="--rw:85%;--k:4"><a class="soc-bar soc-b-commoners soc-est" href="#rank-6" style="--sw:1%"><span class="soc-bar-n"><span class="soc-loc">Neodamodeis</span> <span class="soc-en">(Freed helots)</span></span><span class="soc-bar-s">c. 0.5–1.5% (est.)</span></a></li><li class="soc-row" style="--rw:100%;--k:5"><a class="soc-bar soc-b-dependent soc-est" href="#rank-7" style="--sw:70%"><span class="soc-bar-n"><span class="soc-loc">Heilotes</span> <span class="soc-en">(Helots)</span></span><span class="soc-bar-s">About 70% (the rest, est.)</span></a></li></ol><p class="soc-scale-note">By rank, the ladder is drawn as a pyramid. To scale, each bar is as wide as that rank&#8217;s share of the people. Shares marked est. are estimates where no count survives; their boxes and bars are dashed.</p></section>
