m your land or work as a craftsman or trader, and march with Sparta’s army when called, but you have no voice in how Sparta is ruled.","kid":"The perioikoi were free people who lived in their own towns and made the weapons for Sparta’s army.","rise":"Perioikoi were born to their status. Freed helots could be raised to a standing like theirs, but the agoge, and with it Spartan citizenship, was closed to their sons except by rare special permission.","why":"The perioikoi, “those who dwell around”, were free Lacedaemonians who lived in their own towns, at least 33 of them in Laconia and Messenia.","people":[]},{"n":6,"lv":5,"band":"commoners","name":"Freed helots","loc":"Neodamodeis","term":"","lbl":"c. 0.5–1.5% (est.)","w":1,"firm":0,"est":1,"pic":"/images/societies/thumbs/sparta-6.jpg","you":"You were born a helot and won your freedom by serving as a hoplite; you may be sent to fight far from home, and you will never be a citizen.","kid":"Some helots were set free after serving as soldiers in Sparta’s army.","rise":"Freedom came only by decision of the state, chiefly as the reward for service as a hoplite; it made a helot free, but never a citizen.","why":"From the late 5th century Sparta freed helots in return for service as hoplites.","people":[]},{"n":7,"lv":6,"band":"dependent","name":"Helots","loc":"Heilotes","term":"","lbl":"About 70% (the rest, est.)","w":70.2,"firm":1,"est":1,"pic":"/images/societies/thumbs/sparta-7.jpg","you":"You and your family farm a Spartiate’s land and hand over part of the harvest, keeping the rest, and every year the ephors declare war on your people.","kid":"Helots were people conquered by Sparta and forced to farm the land for Spartan citizens.","rise":"Helots were born into their condition. Freedom came only from the state, chiefly as a reward for service as soldiers, until the Theban invasion that followed Leuctra freed the helots of Messenia in 370–369 BCE.","why":"The helots were the subject people of Laconia and Messenia, descended from Greeks conquered by Sparta, above all the Messenians.","people":[]}]}</script>
